# Working notes
stage 1: implemented parse_amount with ordered steps (sign/parens -> optional $ -> two regex shapes for magnitude) and format_amount using divmod + "{:,}" with sign before "$"; one-digit fractions right-padded, negative zero returns 0.
stage 2: parse_line enforces exactly-3 fields, date shape regex AND real-calendar check (fromisoformat alone is insufficient), non-empty desc, and converts money's ValueError to LedgerError at the single conversion point; parse_lines returns a 2-tuple with 1-based linenos counting skipped lines.
stage 3: load_rules skips only ";" comments ("#" is a real rule line per spec/00b), requires exactly three "=" parts, lets int() raise naturally for bad priorities; categorize uses case-insensitive substring match, highest priority wins, strict > keeps the earlier rule on ties.
stage 4: summarize groups by category and sorts by (total ascending, category name ascending with plain case-sensitive str); render_report renders in given order with exact 15/12/6 ljust/rjust columns, no truncation, no trailing newline, four lines even when empty.
stage 5: parse_line now accepts 3 or 4 fields; tags split on ",", stripped, lower-cased, empties dropped (trailing comma harmless); categorize treats "#" patterns as exact lower-cased tag equality (never substring), desc rules unchanged.
stage 6: cli.main uses argparse with positional "report" command, reads both files before any parsing (OSError -> "cannot read <path>", exit 2), then load_rules (ValueError -> "rules error:", exit 2), strict errors to stderr with exit 1 and no stdout, non-strict warnings after the report with exit 0.
